<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" /><meta name="description" content="Sources, artwork credits, and simulation limits for Inferno Tips." /><title>Credits & sources — Inferno Tips</title><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" /></head><body><main class="credits-page"><a href="/">← Back to the practice grounds</a><h1>Built for the community.<br />With credit to the community.</h1><p>Inferno Tips is an independent fan-made learning tool. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or operated by Jagex or the creators linked here.</p><h2>Game artwork</h2><p>RuneScape, Old School RuneScape, and game artwork are © Jagex Ltd. Their inclusion identifies the game’s creatures and protection prayers. No ownership of these assets is claimed.</p><ul><li>Protection prayer icons: <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/File:Protect_from_Magic.png">Protect from Magic</a>, <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/File:Protect_from_Missiles.png">Protect from Missiles</a>, and <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/File:Protect_from_Melee.png">Protect from Melee</a>, via the OSRS Wiki and our companion Inferno LoS project.</li><li>Blob, mager, and ranger images: Jagex game artwork distributed in <a href="https://github.com/OldSchoolSDK/InfernoTrainer/tree/06fc103f70f1fa228678ca79910a8d3bb0798a7d/src/content/inferno/assets/images">OldSchoolSDK’s Inferno Trainer</a>. See its <a href="https://github.com/OldSchoolSDK/InfernoTrainer/blob/06fc103f70f1fa228678ca79910a8d3bb0798a7d/assets.md">asset attribution</a>.</li><li>Player image: game artwork via <a href="https://github.com/Supalosa/osrs-colosseum/blob/5b1734f06e0580bcc9cb8a0a681c93a13adaf3d3/public/player.png">Supalosa’s Colosseum tool</a>.</li></ul><h2>Mechanics and further learning</h2><ul><li><a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Inferno/Strategies">OSRS Wiki: Inferno strategies</a> — reference for game tick duration, blob scanning, and enemy attack intervals. The exercises, teaching sequence, and feedback here are original.</li><li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6trKOSUr4EM">Gnomonkey: INFERNO IS FREE NOW! Bofa Guide (OSRS)</a> — a recommended full-run guide, published 3 October 2024. Linked to its original creator; videos and transcripts are not reproduced here.</li><li><a href="https://los.inferno.tips/">Inferno LoS</a> — our companion tool for wave layouts and positioning.</li></ul><h2>What the drills model</h2><p>A challenge tick lasts 600 ms; guided practice uses 900 ms. Blobs read prayer on tick 1 and every six ticks thereafter, then attack with the opposite style three ticks later. With no protection prayer, the exercise chooses a reproducible style; that is a practice choice, not a prediction of the game. Magers and rangers use four-tick attacks. Stack exercises begin with a fixed two-tick offset.</p><p>Rhythm and alternation lessons score their requested pattern. Blob lessons score both controlled reads and protected attacks. Other lessons score attack checks and, where applicable, movement targets. A score is correct checks divided by total checks; it does not measure damage, prayer drain, or real-world latency.</p><p>The marked tile exercise is an invented coordination drill, not an Inferno floor hazard. Click movement places the player directly on the chosen tile, without pathfinding. These exercises do not model combat damage, gear, supplies, melee range, full wave solving, Jad, or Zuk. Use the linked guides and simulator to continue learning.</p><h2>Your progress</h2><p>Completed runs and scores are saved in this browser’s local storage. Guided or interrupted runs count as practice. Two uninterrupted challenges at 90% or more earn lesson mastery. Mastery is a learning milestone, not a guarantee of an Inferno completion. Hidden tabs and delayed browser timers pause the drill. You can delete local scores on the Your progress page.</p><p>Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts; otherwise the drills and game images run locally after the site has loaded. External resources open only when you follow their links.</p></main></body></html>
